While there are no explicit security vulnerabilities found within this specific unit test code block, it’s important to maintain a secure coding practice even in tests. For instance, if the commands were constructed dynamically using user input or external data sources, they could introduce command injection risks (CWE-78). However, in this context, since all command strings are static and pre-defined within the test, there are no apparent security issues.

