    self.cursor.execute(query, (numberOfLinks,))
    result = self.cursor.fetchall()
    self.remove(result)
    return result
```
In this updated version, the `LIMIT` clause uses a parameterized placeholder (`%s`) and passes `numberOfLinks` as a tuple to the `execute` method, which safely inserts the value into the query.

