4. **Lack of Prepared Statements or Parameterized Queries (CWE-89)** - High Confidence
The use of string formatting within SQL queries increases the risk of SQL injection attacks, as user input is directly embedded into the query string. It would be more secure to utilize parameterized queries or prepared statements when interacting with the database to prevent SQL injection vulnerabilities.

