<analysis>
The provided code block contains a significant security vulnerability. The function `run_interactive_shell_command` uses the `shell=True` parameter when creating a subprocess with `subprocess.Popen`. This practice is inherently insecure and can lead to arbitrary command execution vulnerabilities.

When `shell=True`, the command string is passed through the shell for interpretation, which means that any characters in the command string that have special meaning in the shell (like `&&`, `|`, `<`, `>`, etc.) can be exploited. An attacker could inject malicious code into the `command` parameter to execute arbitrary system commands.

For example, if an attacker provides a command like `"ls && rm -rf /"` as input, it would list the contents of the directory and then recursively delete everything in it.

This vulnerability is classified under CWE-78 (OS Command Injection).

