2. **Unprotected Storage of Credentials**
   The function `shame_add` attempts to store credentials (in this case, a name) in plain text in the `people` table. This is a security risk because if an attacker gains access to the database, they will have access to all stored credentials.

   Although not directly comparable to storing passwords, storing names (which might be unique identifiers or sensitive information) can still pose risks depending on how these are used elsewhere in the application.

