   - Implementing a try-finally block or using context managers (e.g., `with` statement) would ensure that resources are properly released even if an error occurs.

Overall, the most critical issue is the SQL injection vulnerability due to improper handling of user input. This can be addressed by using parameterized queries provided by the database library (in this case, `psycopg2`). 

