Also note that this function runs commands ('tee', 'mkdir') with root privileges (run_as_root=True). This could lead to a privilege escalation vulnerability if there are any flaws in these functions. 

Finally, contents of the `contents` variable are directly written into the file without validation or sanitisation which can potentially result in code injection attacks if user-provided content includes arbitrary commands that would be executed on the system as root. 

