<analysis>
The function `_get_hostvdisk_mappings` uses string formatting (f-string) to construct an SSH command. This potentially leaves the system open to shell injection attacks, where an attacker could manipulate the host name parameter with malicious commands.

Additionally, there is no input validation on the `mapping_line` returned by the ssh command. The function uses a custom method (_get_hdr_dic) that converts lines of output into dictionaries based on a specified delimiter ('!'). If an attacker can control the content of `mapping_line`, they could potentially manipulate the data in unanticipated ways.

Lastly, there is no error handling for situations where the ssh command fails or if it does not return expected output. This could result in silent failures and difficult to diagnose issues. 
</analysis>

