- Secondly, `'/'` check is checking if sid contains a '/', but that would mean there can be file paths traversal attacks as any '/' character input will allow for directory escalation. For example, an attacker might provide the path '../etc/passwd'. If such functionality exists in the application, it may need to be reviewed further and mitigated accordingly.
- Thirdly, the function is sending sensitive files (presumably logs) over HTTP without proper encryption or authentication which can lead to potential eavesdropping attacks. 

